# T-1027: Contravariant annotation accepted by annotation_to_variance.
# [let a@Contravariant] marks parameter `a` as contravariant — accepted by the type system.
# The body [fn: [fn@a []]] is a named-key record annotation (no runtime constructors).
# TypeAlias Callback entry is skipped at runtime — only result: true is present.
# Absence of === warn asserts annotation_to_variance("Contravariant") resolves cleanly.
[
  Callback: [type [let a@Contravariant] [fn: [fn@a []]]]
  result: true
]
=== out
Dict({"result": Bool(true)})
